@startuml storage-layout
title M-UM4: protected layout, owners and descriptor boundary (unimplemented design)
left to right direction

package "Platform root chosen at installation (§4.0)\nexample /opt/swarma; root 0755" {
  folder "libexec/ - root 0755\nswarma-user-manager: v0 accounts, v1 egress\nswarma-user-launcher: dispatcher caller only\nswarma-dispatcher: Unix-socket service from first slice\nswarma-credential-broker: v0 daemon / CLI\nswarma-session-host: SH2+ service-account host\nswarma-session-runner: SH2+ agent-account runner\nfixed protected release paths" as Binaries
  folder "etc/ - root 0755\nuser-manager.json: roles/ranges/metadata retention\napproved-executors.json: paths/digests\nworkspace materialize/export design labels; task exec profiles unpublished\nmachine-owned network + exec selection beside config; exec identity/body pin\n(filename/encoding unpublished)" as Config
  package "lib/user-manager/ - root control state" {
    file "ledger.json - root 0644\nfresh random 128-bit generations forever; UID cursor\nmonotonic store epoch (encoding unpublished)" as Ledger
    folder "receipts/ - root\nstart files 0644\n<generation>/<execution_id>.json" as Receipts
    folder "applied-state/ - root 0644 (§4.0)\nv1 per-generation enforcement metadata" as Applied
    folder "journal/ and lock - root 0700 (§4.0)\nplanned/completed steps; exclusive durable lock" as Journal
  }
  folder "run/ - 0755\ncredential-broker/ (v0), dispatcher/ (first slice)\nsession-host/ (SH2+ activation gated)\nservice socket directories" as Runtime
  folder "services/<account>/ - account owner 0700\nservice home" as ServiceHomes
  folder "Task resources next to workspace\nplatform-materialized read-only; digests in plan\ndata, never instructions; placement unpublished" as Resources
  folder "workers/<account>/ - account owner 0700\nagent/workplace home: work/, tmp/, harness state" as AgentHomes
  folder "quarantine/ - root 0700\nretiring homes moved on same filesystem" as Quarantine
  folder "archive/ - root 0700\nclosed-schema service-generated metadata\nexport files root 0600; naming unpublished" as Archives
}
database "OS directory service\naccount and primary group; manager-created\nmacOS local node / Linux records" as OS
file "Audit log - root-owned\ntime/caller/op/args/result\nexact path unspecified in spec §§4.0, 4.6, 11" as Audit
component "Platform installer\nconfigured installer caller UID; sudo to root" as Installer
component "swarma-user-manager\nroot; one operation / recovery" as M
component "swarma-operator\nprotected service; operator UID\nbroker operator/account owner; signing authority" as Operator
component "swarma-observer\nprotected service; read-only\nno mutation/launcher" as Observer
component "swarma-user-launcher\nroot until groups/GID/UID drop" as L
component "swarma-dispatcher\nservice account swarma-dispatcher" as D
component "swarma-credential-broker\nits service UID; credential state owned by broker" as Broker
component "curator-run -> harness\nagent UID; account-owned content" as Agent
database "Admitted workspace-result + all-blob custody\noutside child home and retirement deletion path\nlocation/transport unpublished (§7)" as Content
component "Kernel firewall\nv0 static UID-range rule; v1 per-account narrowing\nhelper-owned pf parent/account anchors or nftables table" as Firewall

Installer --> Binaries : install protected binaries
Installer --> Config : install policy and approved list
Installer --> Journal : install state directories / sudoers (§11)
Installer --> Firewall : static range deny BEFORE agent accounts; active test-UID precedence probe
Installer --> M : configured service creation for operator/observer (§4.3)
Operator --> M : helper only; authenticated sudo; timestamp_timeout=0
Observer --> Ledger : accounts read without confirmation
M --> Ledger : atomic replace: temp / flush / rename / directory flush
M --> Journal : serialise mutation/recovery/effect.observe; retain effect/removal evidence
M --> Audit : append one operation line
M --> Applied : publish after successful v1 apply
M --> OS : create / remove account and group
M --> ServiceHomes : descriptor-relative create; fchown / fchmod
M --> AgentHomes : descriptor-relative create; no recursive chown
D --> Content : digest/size verify result + EVERY blob, durable complete-content receipt;\ncurrent-authenticated requester retrieval, bounded retention until authenticated import ack/authorized release
M --> Quarantine : only after verified quiescence and complete-content discharge\nor explicit per-act operator waiver; dispatcher owns export obligation
M --> Quarantine : declared keys destroyed BEFORE deletion; bounded batches delete ALL home objects; yield lock;\nfailed/unknown/incomplete keeps retiring and reservations
M --> Archives : export from trusted service records ONLY (schema/provenance gate);\nsweep metadata age then total; preserve live effect/tombstone evidence
M --> Firewall : v1 narrowing before launch; workplace ZERO egress;\naccount-rule cleanup after account/group; static range rule remains
L --> Config : approved path + digest; caller policy
L --> Ledger : active agent / qualified workplace generation; caller owner
L --> Journal : transition lock; bounded dependency recovery; reservations/accounting first
L --> Receipts : atomic root receipt BEFORE privilege drop
L --> Audit : operation audit (§4.6)
L --> AgentHomes : home opened no-follow as cwd
D --> M : sudo; closed helper stdin (effect IDs)
D --> L : sudo; closed launch stdin (launch effect ID)
L --> Agent : only FDs 0-2 and read-only FD3: fully staged bounded immutable plan
Agent --> AgentHomes : prepare work/ and tmp/ as agent UID
Agent --> Broker : fresh broker connection; no inherited connection
Broker --> Ledger : direct read; generation check
Broker --> Applied : direct v1 read; never agent enforcement claim
note bottom of Runtime
  Service socket names, owner/group and socket modes:
  unspecified in spec §4.0; service contracts define them.
  Helper creates service accounts, not broker credential storage (§1.1).
end note
note bottom of Archives
  Ordinary retirement deletes the home; no archive/delete/keep selector (§4.4.1).
  Destroy declared keys before walk; failed/unknown destruction/deletion keeps retiring.
  Retirement metadata export never copies agent-controlled strings/names/links/bodies; service provenance required.
  Export schema/naming/bounds, declared paths and audit encoding open (§14 question 6).
  Separate explicit swarma-operator home retention: authentication + exact-content confirmation;
  refused inside agent sessions; confidentiality not guaranteed; format unpublished (§14 questions 1, 17).
  Broker credentials are outside helper ownership (§1.1).
end note
note bottom of Journal
  Refusal: control path symlink; opened object type/owner/device checked (§6).
  Linux openat2 BENEATH/NO_SYMLINKS; macOS component openat O_NOFOLLOW.
  Dependency recovery compares OS objects; stop/retire continues original effect (§4.6).
  Cleanup batches yield lock; unrelated safe controls proceed; all reservations/accounting validated.
  R-LOCK: no state lock across synchronous platform-service call; in-flight generation fenced.
  Effect/start-receipt/removal evidence retained until permanent inadmissibility (§4.6).
  Concrete retention/coverage rules unpublished (§14 question 8); expiry is unavailable, not absence.
  R-FD3: scrub untrusted inherited FDs before trusted handles; retain generation lock
  through receipt and verified UID/GID drop; verified executable handle through exec.
  Last-use / qualified close-on-exec cleanup; release on every failure (§7).
  Per-platform immutable FD3 staging mechanism/deadlines open (§14 question 7).
end note
note "Defining spec: [[../spec/helper.md#40-layout §4.0 layout]], [[../spec/helper.md#45-userlist-and-the-ledger §4.5 ledger]],\n[[../spec/helper.md#441-retirement-deletion-and-metadata-export §4.4.1 deletion/export]], [[../spec/helper.md#6-file-operations §6 file safety]],\n[[../spec/helper.md#7-the-launcher-swarma-user-launcher §7 descriptor crossing]], [[../spec/helper.md#11-installation §11 install]].\nCurrent: nothing implemented; v0 accounts/launcher, v1 applied state/egress, v2 grants/opt-in ACL (§13).\nOnly explicit spec modes shown; unspecified file/directory modes and group owners remain unspecified (§4.0).\nOS record storage paths/modes: unspecified in spec §4.3 (owned by OS backend).\nSH1 extraction does not activate SH2+ host/runner placement; joint admission gate I4 closed (§§7, 14).\nCompanion components own their binaries/socket contracts; helper installer scope remains §11.\nNo default parent read ACL (§13); no donor provisioning operation (§1.1)." as Scope
Scope .. Ledger
note bottom of Config
  R-NETBIND: name + Curator lock digest -> exactly one pinned network ref/digest.
  No direct/external-http-proxy binding for any platform account class.
  One profile-bound listener per bound account generation; row admits only its own proxy.port.
  Exec relation: Curator identity/lock + placement/class -> one profile identity/body digest.
  Dispatcher prepare pins input/1; launcher verifies body at start/retry, drift refuses.
  fw.apply checks account_generation/profile_ref/service_generation/served_policy_digest.
  Digest covers allow entries/caps/guard version; re-apply reconciles proxy sessions.
  N15 revision 2026-10-13 owns proposed platform-proxy kind/fixed refused-port set (§8).
  R-SVC-EGRESS: installer service rows and separate verification schedule, DNS sandbox gate.
  R-WORKPLACE: fixed root relay shell; rb-exec service controls outside worker home/UID.
end note
note bottom of Ledger
  R-GEN: external restore mark closes ALL direct consumers before restored bytes visible.
  Each reader keeps highest store epoch outside rollback domain; reconcile surviving inventory.
  Retiring/removed never becomes active; pre-restore coverage unavailable until proved.
  Restore mark/floor encoding unpublished; whole-machine rollback not locally detectable.
  R-TRANSFER: cross-account repository private/standalone; no hooks/remotes/helpers.
  Approved workspace materialize before work / export after confirmed UID absence, child UID.
  Dispatcher relays/journals base archive, holds no repository; result only original requester.
  Immutable B manifest: path/Git kind/mode/content; archive verified before work;
  import independently recomputes repository B; mode/type-only modify, deletion prior mode.
  Each physical start has distinct claim/launch/stop/receipt/absence and durable round linkage.
  Bounded original-admission expiry consent collects only while active; no security-hold bypass.
  Refusal immutable; same-workspace repair separately admitted with current authority/budget;
  new linked effects, then tool-write/SSH fences and account-wide absence before re-export.
  Complete result/all-blob custody outside deletion discharges, or explicit per-act waiver.
  Digest-only/incomplete evidence retains obligation; standing discard off.
  Home deletion need not await import; independently retained content requires authenticated
  import acknowledgement or explicit release, never silent expiry/stale-signature retrieval.
  Formats/caps/retention/interlocks unpublished (§14 question 15).
end note
note bottom of Operator
  Neither operator nor observer hosts a harness session; homes under services/, not workers/.
  Installer naming services in policy or configured operator may create them; dispatcher cannot.
  Phone key never leaves secure element; biometric gate; tailnet SSH key-only forced operator command.
  Signed operator record bound to one act; machine verifies against pinned phone key.
  Widening: authentication + exact-content confirmation; CLI refuses inside agent sessions.
  Revocation: single biometric confirmation. Terminal fallback: password sudo, no cached ticket.
  Operator/installer helper rules authenticate; NOPASSWD only dispatcher helper/launcher.
  Read-only observer status/grants/accounts/bindings require no confirmation.
  Other read interfaces, command binary/wire, canonical bytes/domain, exact sshd/OS entry,
  phone-to-helper authenticated transition, key lifecycle and service egress rows unpublished (§14 question 17).
end note
note bottom of Firewall
  R-RANGE-DENY: range 30000-59999; v0 proxy listeners only, v1 account narrowing/zero egress.
  Linux every-protocol skuid counters/logs; macOS pf user range + sandbox beyond TCP/UDP.
  Active precedence probe install/start/schedule; earlier quick on any interface -> incident/readiness drop.
  R-NET-TOOL workplace Linux namespace + Unix-only families; macOS deny-network sandbox + UID deny.
  R-SOCKETS probe proves reachable set equals declared platform sockets; all others unreachable.
  R-ALLSTOP direct same-act range deny-all; root receiver mark before inventory.
  Mark closes create/activation/physical start/ingress, including already-issued effects.
  Receipt-backed stops or fresh never-launched absence with full no-launch coverage.
  Direct helper progress without dispatcher; unknown parts keep admission closed.
  ALL durable service parts precede scoped explicit recovery/hold-last (§8.3).
end note
note bottom of AgentHomes
  R-EXEC writable areas non-executable; full invocation/transitive code inputs qualified.
  Protected fixed entrypoint/config/environment; unsupported tools go to R-VERIFY.
  R-CEILINGS selected Linux non-delegated unit + per-UID agents-filesystem disk quota.
  macOS aggregate APFS quota, per-account disk/memory watcher soft; qualified host matrix.
  R-WATCH least-privilege sampler: CPU/memory/process/home/network/refused counters incl. mail.
  Generation/boot/interval-bound; v0 stop/hold/observer status, no phone/per-account freeze promise.
  v1 freeze lifecycle remains open with S2.
  R-VERIFY builds/tests/code execution only off-host ephemeral secret-free runners.
  R-STANDING trusted local loops verify plan surfaces at every launch/restart/native resume.
  Workplace untrusted by default; operator trusted-circle admission only enables donor-side opt-ins.
  Host zero egress, exec profile, transfer and review stay; web-service sockets refuse workplaces.
  R-UNTRUSTED v0 refusal; v1 ceilings/exec/zero workplace egress/no local loop or subscription lease.
  R-SHARED no shared services beside untrusted work; platform services excluded from shared definition.
end note
note bottom of Resources
  Trusted side gathers/checks task resources and attaches to board; signed-letter attachments for remote.
  More requested by letter/outcome; worker never fetches; formats/caps/plan encoding unpublished (§8).
  Default: no web; donor loop reaches only provider endpoints and our host, our side has no internet.
  Web options default-off; explicit per-identity trusted-circle opt-in only.
  Local web-tool service: own account, row and listener; key outside agent accounts.
  Local agents reach it only over Unix socket with peer-UID admission and grant; never TCP/workplace.
  Donor web service separate from harness/bridge; key never reaches project (§8).
end note
@enduml
